cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the Ashoka University discussion
  paper and the SSRN working paper listed below, and the software itself.
title: "phdid: Partial Homogeneity in Staggered Difference-in-Differences"
version: 0.1.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/ronwag2005/phdid"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Wagle
    given-names: Rohan
    email: rohan.wagle_ug2023@ashoka.edu.in
    affiliation: "Department of Economics, Ashoka University"
  - family-names: Arora
    given-names: Parush
    email: parush.arora@ashoka.edu.in
    affiliation: "Department of Economics, Ashoka University"
abstract: >-
  Estimation and specification testing for staggered difference-in-differences
  designs under partial homogeneity of the cohort-time average treatment
  effects. Implements a Dirichlet process mixture estimator via a collapsed
  Gibbs sampler and an L0-penalised partial-homogeneity estimator, together
  with tests for recoverable heterogeneity, regularisation paths for both
  estimators, and sampler diagnostics including exact partition enumeration.
keywords:
  - difference-in-differences
  - staggered treatment
  - treatment effect heterogeneity
  - Dirichlet process
  - model selection
  - causal inference
  - econometrics
  - R
